# ============================================================
# .dockerignore — What Docker should NEVER upload
# ============================================================
#
# When Docker builds an image, it first packages your entire
# project folder into a "build context" and sends it to the
# Docker daemon. Without this file, it would upload gigabytes
# of node_modules and .git history on every single build.
# This file is the equivalent of .gitignore but for Docker.
# ============================================================

# Version control — Docker doesn't need your git history
.git
.gitignore

# All node_modules — Docker installs them fresh inside the container
**/node_modules

# Build artifacts — we build fresh inside the container
**/dist
**/.next
**/.turbo

# Local environment files — NEVER bake secrets into an image!
# Secrets are injected at runtime by Render's environment variables.
**/.env
**/.env.local
**/.env.*.local

# Editor and OS noise
.vscode
.idea
**/.DS_Store
**/Thumbs.db

# Test coverage reports — not needed in production
**/coverage

# Docker files themselves
**/Dockerfile
**/.dockerignore
